  "fragment": "<div class=\"crunch-bridge\"><p>Next, a little pocket deception.</p><a href=\"#copper\" class=\"text-button\">Keep wandering ↓</a></div>\n<section class=\"copper-story\" id=\"copper\" aria-labelledby=\"copper-title\">\n<div class=\"copper-sticky\">\n<div class=\"copper-question\">\n  <div class=\"question-copy\"><h2 id=\"copper-title\">Which one has<br><span>more copper?</span></h2><p>Pick a coin. Or go straight to the answer.</p><button class=\"round-link\" id=\"reveal\" aria-controls=\"copper-answer\">Show me <span aria-hidden=\"true\">↗</span></button></div>\n  <div class=\"coin-duet\" role=\"group\" aria-label=\"Which coin contains more copper?\">\n    <figure class=\"hero-penny\"><button class=\"coin-choice\" data-coin=\"penny\" aria-label=\"Choose the penny\"><img src=\"assets/penny.webp\" alt=\"\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\" loading=\"lazy\"><span>Penny</span></button></figure>\n    <figure class=\"hero-nickel\"><button class=\"coin-choice\" data-coin=\"nickel\" aria-label=\"Choose the nickel\"><img src=\"assets/nickel.webp\" alt=\"\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\"><span>Nickel</span></button></figure>\n  </div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"copper-answer\" id=\"copper-answer\" hidden>\n  <div class=\"answer-copy\"><p class=\"answer-lead\" id=\"coin-feedback\">The nickel. And it’s not even close.</p><div class=\"giant-ratio\">60<span>×</span></div><h2 id=\"copper-result\" tabindex=\"-1\" aria-label=\"The nickel contains sixty times as much copper as the penny\" aria-describedby=\"coin-feedback\">as much copper.<br>In the silver-looking one.</h2><p>A penny is copper-coated zinc.<br>A nickel is 75% copper.</p><button id=\"again\" class=\"text-button\">See the two coins again ↺</button></div>\n  <div class=\"copper-equation\"><figure class=\"single-nickel\"><img src=\"assets/nickel.webp\" alt=\"One nickel\" width=\"500\" height=\"500\"><figcaption>Copper in<br><strong>one nickel</strong></figcaption></figure><span class=\"equals\" aria-hidden=\"true\">=</span><figure class=\"penny-collection\"><div id=\"penny-pile\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></div><figcaption>Copper in<br><strong>sixty pennies</strong></figcaption></figure><p class=\"equation-note\">Equal copper mass. Not equal spending money.</p></div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"copper-bottom\"><span class=\"tiny-note\">Modern U.S. penny &amp; nickel · copper content by mass</span><details class=\"source\"><summary>The receipts</summary><p><a href=\"https://www.usmint.gov/learn/coins-and-medals/circulating-coins/coin-specifications\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">U.S. Mint specifications ↗</a><br>Penny: 2.5 g × 2.5% = 0.0625 g copper. Nickel: 5 g × 75% = 3.75 g copper. Ratio: 60. Based on rounded specifications, not individual coin measurements. The coin collection compares copper content, not face value or total coin mass.</p></details></div>\n</div>\n</section>\n",
